<Layout title="About the library · Books" active="about"><article class="wrap about"><span class="eyebrow">THE OPEN NOTEBOOK</span><h1>A library of<br/><em>lived-in stories.</em></h1><div class="prose"><p>This is my personal record of books read and audiobooks listened to. It began with an audiobook collection and has room to grow in both directions.</p><h2>Two ways into a story</h2><p><strong>Listened</strong> means I’ve listened to the audiobook. <strong>Read</strong> means I’ve read the book. <strong>Read & listened</strong> means both. An unrecorded reading status doesn’t mean I haven’t read it; that part of the notebook is still being filled in.</p><h2>A shelf, not a completion checklist</h2><p>Series pages show the titles in my collection, including short stories and companion works. Missing volumes aren’t a statement about the series. Alternate narrations and multi-disc recordings share a single entry wherever they represent the same work.</p><h2>About the covers and descriptions</h2><p>Descriptions focus on the setup and themes, leaving discoveries to the story. Cover images come from public book sources, with US editions preferred when the edition’s publication location can be confirmed. Some editions have no available cover; those get a simple typographic jacket.</p><h2>A little notebook underneath</h2><p>The library is maintained as Markdown files in <a href="https://github.com/jugglingbear/books">the Books repository</a>. It’s built with Astro and published on GitHub Pages. Search happens in your browser.</p></div></article></Layout>
